// **a decision on record, not a feature.** a write through a `T&` bound to a literal lands in storage
// nobody will read again, and the compiler does not refuse it: it cannot tell a mutating callee from a
// reading one, and Echo already has the spelling that says which - `const T&`
//
// gating the rank on constness instead would refuse every borrow parameter in the stdlib, which are
// written bare. so the program compiles, the write happens, and it is simply unobservable

function bump(int32& $x) : void
{
    $x = $x + 100;
}

bump(1);
echo 7;
